        <headline>Small Craft Advisory issued September 24 at 2:05AM EDT until September 25 at 8:00AM EDT by NWS Boston/Norton MA</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...For the Small Craft Advisory, northeast winds 15 to 25
kt with gusts up to 35 kt and waves 2 to 3 feet. For the Gale
Warning, north winds 20 to 30 kt with gusts up to 40 kt and
waves around 3 feet expected.

* WHERE...Narragansett Bay.

* WHEN...For the Small Craft Advisory, until 8 AM EDT Friday.
For the Gale Warning, from 8 AM Friday to 8 PM EDT Saturday.

* IMPACTS...Strong winds will cause hazardous waves which could
capsize or damage vessels and reduce visibility.
</description>
        <instruction>Mariners should alter plans to avoid these hazardous conditions.
Remain in port, seek safe harbor, alter course, and/or secure the
vessel for hazardous conditions.</instruction>
